## 4. F3 — CLOSED, and the mutation proves it is not cosmetic.

The fixture was rewritten on W-069's own priming recipe. The two defects I
named are both gone:

  - the second battery is fed `only: pairs` — the SAME full candidate set —
    never `capped.skipped`. Nothing is fed forward from a prior result, so
    "probes exactly those" can no longer be true by construction.
  - the five test pairs carry DISTINCT primed `at` values (each primed by its
    own single-candidate battery at `later(NOW, i*1000)`), so the sort has
    something real to order. A dedicated seated control (`aaa-ctrl`)
    decouples the control's own turn from the property under test.
  - every assertion reads the actual `calls.start` SEQUENCE or the record's
    own state.

Standalone run, verbatim:

  PASS  b3 w071: capped run makes exactly 2 start calls         ["aaa-ctrl","codex-p1"]
  PASS  b3 w071: control runs first, then the single OLDEST test pair
  PASS  b3 w071: the 4 fresher test pairs come back in skipped  ["codex-p2","codex-p3","codex-p4","codex-p5"]
  PASS  b3 w071: run two's control runs first                   ["aaa-ctrl","codex-p2","codex-p3","codex-p4","codex-p5","codex-p1"]
  PASS  b3 w071: run two heads with the previously-stranded pair (codex-p2), not codex-p1
  PASS  b3 w071: run two positive control — the pair already turned in run one (codex-p1) is probed LAST
  PASS  b3 w071: positive control — no cap yields 6 start calls and an empty skipped   6

Traced independently to confirm the fixture discriminates rather than merely
passes. After priming, ages are p1=+0 (oldest) … p5=+4000, aaa-ctrl=+4000.
Run one (cap 2) must spend the control then p1 only. Run one leaves p1 at
+10000 — the FRESHEST — so run two's age order is p2,p3,p4,p5,p1 while both
alphabetical and insertion order are p1,p2,p3,p4,p5. `order2[1] === "codex-p2"`
and `order2[last] === "codex-p1"` therefore fail under either wrong order.
The discrimination is carried by run two, exactly as the fixture's own comment
claims; run one alone could not tell age order from alphabetical, and does not
pretend to.

